
use the following function in CubeIde to write in the file values.txt

void filePrintDistance(int distance) {
    // Open file in append mode (creates if doesn't exist)
	
	char* filepath = "/home/fede/Desktop/Embedded_Platform/TOF_LinearRegression/values.txt";
	
    FILE* file = fopen(filepath, "a");
    if (file == NULL) {
        printf("Error opening file %s\r\n", filepath);
        return;
    }
    
    // Write the distance measurement
    fprintf(file, "%d\n", distance);
    
    // Close the file
    fclose(file);
}

USAGE:
-modify filepath
- use: filePrintDistance(distance1);

then use linReg.py to read those values and compute lin reg coefficients

